**DEFECT 1: Signature mismatch between header declaration and implementation — compile error**

**File:** `src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawViewPart.h` lines 242–244 (declared) vs `src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawViewPart.cpp` lines 1501–1506 (defined)

The header declares all three methods as **`static`** with **two parameters**:

```cpp
static bool isCosmeticVertex(App::DocumentObject* owner, std::string element);
static bool isCosmeticEdge(App::DocumentObject* owner, std::string element);
static bool isCenterLine(App::DocumentObject* owner, std::string element);
```

The .cpp defines them as **non-static** with **one parameter**:

```cpp
bool DrawViewPart::isCosmeticVertex(std::string element) { ... }
bool DrawViewPart::isCosmeticEdge(std::string element) { ... }
bool DrawViewPart::isCenterLine(std::string element) { ... }
```

These are entirely different signatures. The compiler will reject the definitions because they don't match any declaration in the class. Any call site using the header's 2-parameter static form will get an unresolved-symbol linker error; any call site trying to use the 1-parameter non-static form from the header won't find a declaration at all. **This code does not compile.**

The implementations in the .cpp are logically correct — they call `this->getProjVertexByIndex()` / `this->getEdge()` directly and don't need the old `owner` parameter. The header is the one that was not updated to match.

**DEFECT 1: Signature mismatch between header declaration and implementation in DrawViewPart**

**File:** `src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawViewPart.h` (lines 242-244) vs `src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawViewPart.cpp` (lines 1501, 1513, 1525)

**Failure scenario:** Any compilation of this code will fail. The header declares three `static` methods taking `(App::DocumentObject* owner, std::string element)`, but the `.cpp` defines them as non-static member functions taking only `(std::string element)`.

```cpp
// DrawViewPart.h:242-244
static bool isCosmeticVertex(App::DocumentObject* owner, std::string element);
static bool isCosmeticEdge(App::DocumentObject* owner, std::string element);
static bool isCenterLine(App::DocumentObject* owner, std::string element);

// DrawViewPart.cpp:1501, 1513, 1525
bool DrawViewPart::isCosmeticVertex(std::string element)  // missing 'static', missing owner param
bool DrawViewPart::isCosmeticEdge(std::string element)
bool DrawViewPart::isCenterLine(std::string element)
```

**Concrete result:** Linker errors (undefined references to the static versions) or compiler errors (redefinition with different signatures), depending on whether the static declarations are treated as separate declarations.
